---
const privacyEmail = "rahul@takovibe.com";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
        <title>FocusLock / ZenMode Privacy Policy</title>
        <meta
            name="description"
            content="Privacy policy for the FocusLock / ZenMode Android app by TakoVibe."
        />
        <style>
            body {
                max-width: 760px;
                margin: 2rem auto;
                padding: 0 1rem;
                font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
                line-height: 1.6;
                color: #222;
            }
            h1 { font-size: 2.2rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
            h2 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
            h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.75rem; }
            code {
                background: #f2f2f2;
                padding: 1px 5px;
                border-radius: 3px;
                font-size: 0.9em;
            }
            a { color: #c2410c; }
        </style>
    </head>
    <body>
        <h1>Privacy Policy for FocusLock / ZenMode</h1>
        <p>Last updated: June 22, 2026</p>

        <p>
            FocusLock, also referred to as ZenMode by its Android package name
            <code>com.takovibe.zenmode</code>, is a focus and app-locking app developed by TakoVibe.
            This Privacy Policy explains what information FocusLock accesses, collects, uses,
            shares, and retains.
        </p>

        <p>
            Privacy contact: <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>
        </p>

        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
            FocusLock is designed to help you start and protect focus sessions. We do not sell
            personal or sensitive user data. We do not use your selected app list, accessibility
            events, focus sessions, or device permission data for advertising.
        </p>
        <p>
            Most FocusLock data stays on your device unless you choose to sign in for cloud backup,
            use Google Play purchases, or use Google services that are part of the app such as
            Firebase Analytics, Remote Config, in-app updates, or in-app review prompts.
        </p>

        <h2>Information FocusLock Accesses or Collects</h2>

        <h3>Focus session and settings data</h3>
        <p>FocusLock stores the settings and session data needed to run the app, including:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>focus session start and end times;</li>
            <li>session duration, completion status, streaks, and focus statistics;</li>
            <li>focus profiles and schedules;</li>
            <li>selected available apps, blocked apps, and emergency apps;</li>
            <li>
                preferences such as Do Not Disturb behavior, strict protection, break settings,
                always-on display settings, scene choices, and ambient player settings.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            This data is used to run focus sessions, show progress and insights, restore app state,
            and keep your configured routines working.
        </p>

        <h3>Installed app information</h3>
        <p>
            FocusLock shows a list of launchable apps on your device so you can choose which apps
            are available, blocked, or treated as emergency apps during focus sessions. On Android
            11 and later, FocusLock uses scoped package visibility through manifest
            <code>&lt;queries&gt;</code> for launcher and essential app intents. FocusLock does not
            request the broad <code>QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES</code> permission.
        </p>
        <p>
            The app names and package names you select may be stored locally. If you sign in and
            enable cloud backup, selected package names and profile data are backed up to Firebase
            Firestore so they can be restored on your devices. We do not sell installed-app
            information, and we do not share it for advertising or analytics monetization.
        </p>

        <h3>Accessibility Service data</h3>
        <p>
            FocusLock uses Android's Accessibility Service only when you enable it and only to
            support focus blocking. During an active Light Mode focus session, the service observes
            foreground-app change events so FocusLock can return you to the focus screen if you open
            an app that is not allowed for that session.
        </p>
        <p>FocusLock's Accessibility Service:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>reads the package name of the app that comes to the foreground during an active session;</li>
            <li>does not retrieve or read screen text or screen content;</li>
            <li>does not record audio, capture screenshots, or log keystrokes;</li>
            <li>does not use accessibility data for advertising;</li>
            <li>does not sell or share accessibility data.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The Accessibility Service is used only for the user-facing focus-lock feature described in the app.</p>

        <h3>Device Admin</h3>
        <p>
            FocusLock may offer optional Device Admin protection for strict focus sessions. If you
            enable it, Device Admin is used to make it harder to remove the app during a protected
            focus session. FocusLock does not use Device Admin to erase your device, change your
            device password, or manage your device for enterprise purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
            You can disable Device Admin from Android system settings when a protected session is
            not preventing removal.
        </p>

        <h3>Do Not Disturb, notifications, battery, boot, widget, and quick settings access</h3>
        <p>FocusLock may request or use these Android permissions and APIs:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Notification permission, to show focus session status and timer notifications.</li>
            <li>Notification Policy Access, to enable Do Not Disturb during a session if you choose that setting.</li>
            <li>Foreground Service, to keep an active focus session running.</li>
            <li>Ignore Battery Optimizations, to reduce the chance that Android stops a long focus session.</li>
            <li>Receive Boot Completed, to re-arm scheduled focus sessions after your device restarts.</li>
            <li>App Widget and Quick Settings Tile APIs, to let you start or view focus sessions from Android surfaces.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These permissions are used only for FocusLock's core focus-session functionality.</p>

        <h3>Account and cloud backup data</h3>
        <p>
            If you choose to sign in with Google, FocusLock uses Google Sign-In and Firebase
            Authentication. We may receive your Firebase user ID, display name, email address, and
            profile photo URL from Google Sign-In. This is used to authenticate you and connect your
            app data to your backup account.
        </p>
        <p>
            When cloud backup is active, FocusLock stores backup data in Firebase Firestore,
            including settings, profiles, selected app package names, schedules, focus statistics,
            and recent session history. Raw session history stored in the cloud is limited by the
            app to approximately one year. Other account backup data is kept until it is deleted as
            described below.
        </p>
        <p>
            Signing out stops account sync on that device, but it may not automatically delete cloud
            backup data already stored for your account.
        </p>

        <h3>Analytics and diagnostics</h3>
        <p>
            FocusLock uses Firebase Analytics for coarse product analytics, such as onboarding
            progress, whether key permissions were granted, app selection counts, first session
            start/completion/abandonment, session duration, commitment level, and launch source.
            These events are used to understand app reliability and improve the onboarding and focus
            experience.
        </p>
        <p>
            FocusLock analytics are intentionally coarse. We do not send the actual list of apps you
            selected to Firebase Analytics.
        </p>
        <p>
            FocusLock may also use Firebase Remote Config to fetch app configuration such as update
            messages, feature limits, pricing presentation, or minimum supported app version.
        </p>

        <h3>Purchases</h3>
        <p>
            FocusLock uses Google Play Billing for Pro upgrades, subscriptions, lifetime purchases,
            and any optional paid early-exit purchase if that feature is enabled. Google Play
            processes payment information. FocusLock receives purchase status, product IDs, purchase
            tokens, and entitlement state from Google Play so the app can unlock paid features,
            restore purchases, or consume eligible one-time products.
        </p>
        <p>FocusLock does not collect or store your credit card number or full payment details.</p>

        <h3>Updates and reviews</h3>
        <p>
            FocusLock may use Google Play's in-app update and in-app review APIs. These services are
            provided by Google Play and are used to help keep the app updated and to request reviews
            at appropriate moments.
        </p>

        <h3>Android and Google backup</h3>
        <p>
            FocusLock allows Android backup. Depending on your device settings and Android version,
            Android or Google system backup may back up local app data so it can be restored later.
            This is separate from FocusLock's optional Firebase cloud backup.
        </p>

        <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>We use information to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>run and protect focus sessions;</li>
            <li>enforce your selected available, blocked, and emergency app rules;</li>
            <li>show progress, streaks, and insights;</li>
            <li>support schedules, widgets, quick settings, notifications, and Do Not Disturb settings;</li>
            <li>provide optional cloud backup and restore;</li>
            <li>authenticate Google sign-in;</li>
            <li>process purchases and restore paid entitlements;</li>
            <li>improve app reliability, onboarding, and feature design;</li>
            <li>provide app updates, app review prompts, support, security, and fraud prevention;</li>
            <li>comply with legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Sharing</h2>
        <p>We do not sell personal or sensitive user data.</p>
        <p>We may share or process data with service providers only as needed to operate the app:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Google Firebase Authentication, Firestore, Analytics, and Remote Config;</li>
            <li>Google Sign-In;</li>
            <li>Google Play Billing;</li>
            <li>Google Play in-app updates and reviews;</li>
            <li>Android system services required for permissions, notifications, accessibility, Device Admin, widgets, quick settings, and Do Not Disturb.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            These providers process data under their own terms and privacy policies. We may also
            disclose information if required by law, legal process, security needs, or to protect
            users, the app, or the public.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
            We use platform and service-provider security controls to protect data. Cloud data is
            transmitted using modern encrypted connections such as HTTPS/TLS. Local data is stored
            in Android app-private storage where Android app sandbox protections apply.
        </p>
        <p>
            No method of storage or transmission is completely secure, but we limit data access and
            collection to what is needed for FocusLock's disclosed functionality.
        </p>

        <h2>Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <p>
            Local app data remains on your device until you delete it in the app if a deletion
            option is available, clear app storage, uninstall FocusLock, or use Android system
            controls that remove app data.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you use cloud backup, account backup data remains in Firebase until it is deleted.
            Raw cloud session history is limited by the app to approximately one year. To request
            deletion of cloud backup data associated with your FocusLock account, contact
            <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a> from the Google account email used
            for FocusLock sign-in. We may retain limited records where required for legal, security,
            fraud prevention, tax, accounting, or purchase dispute purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
            Google Play purchase records are managed by Google Play and may be retained by Google
            according to Google's policies. Firebase Analytics events and aggregated reports may be
            retained according to the analytics retention settings configured for the Firebase
            project and may not identify you directly.
        </p>

        <h2>Your Choices</h2>
        <p>You can:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>decline optional permissions, although some focus-lock features may not work without the permissions they require;</li>
            <li>disable Accessibility Service access in Android settings;</li>
            <li>disable Device Admin access in Android settings when allowed by the current protection state;</li>
            <li>change or disable Do Not Disturb behavior in FocusLock settings and Android settings;</li>
            <li>disable notifications in Android settings;</li>
            <li>sign out of Google account sync in the app;</li>
            <li>clear local data or uninstall FocusLock;</li>
            <li>request deletion of cloud backup data by contacting the privacy contact above.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
            FocusLock is not directed to children. If you believe a child has provided personal
            information through FocusLock, contact us so we can review and delete it where
            appropriate.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy when the app, our data practices, or legal
            requirements change. The updated policy will show a new "Last updated" date.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            For privacy questions or deletion requests, contact:
            <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>
        </p>
    </body>
</html>
